# Owners of the release + supply-chain surface (processes/cli-release.md gate 4).
#
# A `cli-v*` tag runs release-cli.yml with `contents: write` and the
# HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN, and whatever it builds is what `brew install` hands to
# users. Weakening that pipeline should not be a one-person edit.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT THIS ACTUALLY DOES: on its own, CODEOWNERS only auto-requests a
# review — it does not block a merge. It becomes a gate only once branch
# protection on `main` turns on "Require review from Code Owners", which is a
# repo-settings change and therefore operator-only (tracked in backlog/now.md
# alongside the branch-protection item). This file is the half that can live in
# the repo; it is deliberately landed first so the setting has something to
# point at.

# The release pipeline and the formula it publishes.
/.github/workflows/release-cli.yml       @patjackson52
/.github/workflows/release-cli-edge.yml  @patjackson52
/apps/cli/homebrew/                      @patjackson52

